-- חוזר לבעלויות תשע"ה/6 (14.7.2015): תשלום שכר לעובדי הוראה שאינם מחוייבים בהחזר של 4 ימי חופשה בשנה"ל תשע"ה
-- The four working days added in 2014-15 to make up for the four extra
-- vacation days of 2013-14, who is not bound to make them up (staff on full
-- unpaid leave or sabbatical in 2013-14, and new staff), and the pay of
-- those who worked them anyway: their hours on those days at the rate of
-- single substitution hours.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT common

§ `חוזר לבעלויות תשע"ה/6 — תשלום עבור 4 ימי ההחזר בשנה"ל תשע"ה`

-- akn:preamble The letterhead, the date (14.7.2015), the reference number, the addressee, the greeting and the subject; its last paragraph (the background) is encoded below.

DECLARE `make-up action` IS ONE OF
    `work the make-up days`
    `pay for the hours worked on the make-up days` HAS `make-up pay` IS A NUMBER

-- The background: in 2013-14 the staff had four extra vacation days, to
-- open 2014-15 on 27.8.2014; since 2014-15 opened on 1.9.2014, four working
-- days were added against them during 2014-15.
@ref akn:preamble/p14
`the number of make-up days` MEANS 4

-- §1: two days of the Hanukkah recess, 18.12.2014 and 24.12.2014; §2: two
-- days of the Passover recess, 26.3.2015 and 27.3.2015.
@ref akn:art_1 akn:art_2
`the make-up days` MEANS
    LIST Date 18 12 2014, Date 24 12 2014, Date 26 3 2015, Date 27 3 2015

#ASSERT count `the make-up days` EQUALS `the number of make-up days`

@desc A teaching employee's 2013-14 and 2014-15, as far as the make-up days ask about them.
DECLARE `make-up case` HAS
    `on full unpaid leave or full sabbatical in 2013-14` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a new teaching employee`                           IS A BOOLEAN @desc "עובד הוראה חדש"; the circular gives as its reason that such staff were not employed in 2013-14
    `employed in 2013-14 but not when the extra vacation days were given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc employed during 2013-14, but not on the extra vacation days (the circular does not date them)
    `hours worked on the make-up days`                  IS A NUMBER
    `single substitution hour rate`                     IS A NUMBER  @desc the rate of a single substitution hour; an input

-- §2 ¶1: staff on full unpaid leave or sabbatical in 2013-14, and new staff,
-- are not bound to make up the four days, not having been employed in
-- 2013-14 nor had the extra vacation. F-2014-15_tashae_06-a: the categories
-- are what the encoding reads as the rule; the reason is read as explaining
-- them.
@ref akn:art_2/p1
GIVEN c IS A `make-up case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `bound to make up the four days` c IF
        NOT c's `on full unpaid leave or full sabbatical in 2013-14`
    AND NOT c's `a new teaching employee`

-- The same paragraph: those not bound who worked on those days in 2014-15
-- are paid for their hours on them at the rate of single substitution hours.
GIVEN c IS A `make-up case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `pay for the make-up days` c IS
    IF `bound to make up the four days` c
    THEN 0
    ELSE c's `hours worked on the make-up days` TIMES c's `single substitution hour rate`

-- Time in school months of 2014-15 (September 2014 = 1): the last make-up
-- day, 27.3.2015, falls in March (7). The circular names no date for the
-- payment.
GIVEN c IS A `make-up case`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `make-up action`
DECIDE `the make-up days` c IS
    IF `bound to make up the four days` c
    THEN PARTY `the teaching employee`
         MUST  `work the make-up days`
         WITHIN `month number` March
         LEST BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "circular 2014-15/6: four working days were added in 2014-15 against the extra vacation days of 2013-14"
    ELSE IF `pay for the make-up days` c GREATER THAN 0
         THEN PARTY `the employer`
              MUST  `pay for the hours worked on the make-up days` `amount`
                    PROVIDED `amount` AT LEAST `pay for the make-up days` c
         ELSE FULFILLED

-- F-2014-15_tashae_06-a: an employee who worked part of 2013-14 but was not
-- employed when the extra vacation days were given did not have them — the
-- reason the circular gives for releasing staff — yet is neither on a full
-- year's leave nor, by that reason ("not employed in 2013-14"), new.
GIVEN c IS A `make-up case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `released by the reason the circular gives` c IF
    c's `employed in 2013-14 but not when the extra vacation days were given`
    OR c's `on full unpaid leave or full sabbatical in 2013-14`
    OR c's `a new teaching employee`

`a teacher hired in 2013-14 after the extra vacation days` MEANS
    `make-up case` WITH
        `on full unpaid leave or full sabbatical in 2013-14` IS FALSE
        `a new teaching employee`                           IS FALSE
        `employed in 2013-14 but not when the extra vacation days were given` IS TRUE
        `hours worked on the make-up days`                  IS 20
        `single substitution hour rate`                     IS 100

`the reason and the categories part on a teacher hired after the extra days` MEANS
        `released by the reason the circular gives` `a teacher hired in 2013-14 after the extra vacation days`
    AND `bound to make up the four days` `a teacher hired in 2013-14 after the extra vacation days`
#ASSERT `the reason and the categories part on a teacher hired after the extra days`

-- akn:conclusions The contact line, the signature (Sonia Peretz) and the list of copies; no rule.

-- Worked example; the rate of 100 is a placeholder.
`a new teacher who worked 20 hours on those days` MEANS
    `make-up case` WITH
        `on full unpaid leave or full sabbatical in 2013-14` IS FALSE
        `a new teaching employee`                           IS TRUE
        `employed in 2013-14 but not when the extra vacation days were given` IS FALSE
        `hours worked on the make-up days`                  IS 20
        `single substitution hour rate`                     IS 100

#ASSERT `pay for the make-up days` `a new teacher who worked 20 hours on those days` EQUALS 2000
#ASSERT `pay for the make-up days` `a teacher hired in 2013-14 after the extra vacation days` EQUALS 0

#TRACE `the make-up days` `a new teacher who worked 20 hours on those days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay for the hours worked on the make-up days` 2000 AT 1
#TRACE `the make-up days` `a teacher hired in 2013-14 after the extra vacation days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the teaching employee` DOES `work the make-up days` AT 4
